# Part 11's control arm RUNS this program (panel 226's R1, 2026-10-20): the
# strict build refuses it under `cell_redeclared`, a thesis rule, and the control arm,
# `build --permissive`, gives the dropped rule the meaning the sitting's
# table pins: `v @= 2` on a cell already declared is the write `v @ 2`: the next read sees it.
# The witness is the compiler-engineer's (w18-cell_redeclared), one of 27 it ran before the
# resolution was written (`docs/panel/226-reports/compiler-engineer.md`).

function main()
    v: i64 @= 1
    v @= 2  #~ cell_redeclared
    print(v)
